data.content:
## Breaking Changes in Microsoft.OpenApi v2 (shipped with .NET 10)

The `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 package upgraded its dependency from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1** to **v2**, which has several breaking changes:

| What changed | Why |
|---|---|
| `IOpenApiAny` / `OpenApiString` etc. removed | `Example` is now `JsonNode` |
| `Schema.Nullable` removed | OpenAPI 3.1 uses JSON Schema's type array instead |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a `Dictionary` | Now exposes a `Schemes` property |
| `ReferenceType` enum removed | `OpenApiReference` uses string-based `Type` |

---

### Fixed code:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString → JsonNode
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Id = "oauth2", Type = "securityScheme" }
    };

    // No longer a dictionary — use the Schemes property
    var requirement = new OpenApiSecurityRequirement();
    requirement.Schemes.Add(oAuthScheme, scopes);
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement> { requirement };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable removed — instead, remove "null" from the type flags
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of each fix:

1. **`OpenApiString("1.0")`** → `JsonValue.Create("1.0")` — add `using System.Text.Json.Nodes;`, remove `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;`
2. **`OpenApiReference.Type`** → now a `string` (`"securityScheme"`) instead of the `ReferenceType` enum
3. **`new() { [scheme] = scopes }`** → create an `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` and call `.Schemes.Add(scheme, scopes)`
4. **`property.Value.Nullable = false`** → clear the null flag: `property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null`
